WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.720
The end is finally here, and the fate of Hawkins&nbsp;
has never been more perilous. With Max in a coma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:12.160
the gates to the Upside Down completely open, and&nbsp;
the mystery surrounding the Soviets' role in all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:17.200
of it, it's time to explain what went down during&nbsp;
the ending of Season 4 of "Stranger Things."

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.080
The final images of "Stranger Things 4" show us&nbsp;
an escalation of Vecna's assault on Hawkins. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:23.680
started as a series of rifts opening beneath the&nbsp;
town expands to include the familiar, snow-like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:29.120
particles of the Upside Down drifting into the&nbsp;
real world, while the rifts begin to bellow smoke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:34.720
and red lightning crackles in the clouds over the&nbsp;
city. Our heroes know very well what this means,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:40.000
even if no one else in town does. Something&nbsp;
bigger is coming to Hawkins, and soon.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.720
The question that remains as the season ends,&nbsp;
though, is what exactly that bigger something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.280
will look like. We've become very familiar&nbsp;
with the various kinds of creatures who exist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:54.240
in the Upside Down over the years, so is Vecna&nbsp;
simply going to stage an all-out assault with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.040
as many of those beasts as he can summon? Is he&nbsp;
going to bring the Mind Flayer to colossal life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:04.320
over the Hawkins skyline? This is what our heroes&nbsp;
have to figure out as they head into Season 5.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:10.000
Mike and Eleven began Season 4 with serious issues&nbsp;
in their relationship. For Mike, a big part of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.200
problem was not just the physical distance from&nbsp;
El, who moved to California with the Byers family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:20.240
but a perceived distance in their personalities.&nbsp;
For him, El is an exceptional person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:25.920
and he's simply not, and he's sure that one day&nbsp;
she'll realize that and decide she doesn't need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.160
him. For El, who's been struggling with the&nbsp;
loss of her powers at the end of Season 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:34.800
the problem is that she believes Mike doesn't&nbsp;
feel as strongly about her as she feels about him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:39.840
She thinks her outsider status has made her into&nbsp;
a kind of monster that she can never rehabilitate.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.960
By the end of the season, they both&nbsp;
learn they're wrong. Will helps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.000
convince Mike that he's vital&nbsp;
to their entire friend group,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.440
and Eleven's life, as the heart of the party and&nbsp;
the person who keeps everyone buoyed by hope.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.280
"See how you're leading us here? You're&nbsp;
guiding the whole party and inspiring us.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.000
That…that's what you do."

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.280
Through her work with Dr. Brenner, Eleven&nbsp;
comes to realize that she's not a monster and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:06.400
that she's simply been manipulated into perceiving&nbsp;
some kind of wrongness in her mind and body. That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:11.440
leads to an emotional reunion and reconciliation&nbsp;
at the end of the season, but the happiness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:16.160
is short-lived. Will they get a happy ending,&nbsp;
or are they destined to be ripped apart again?

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.680
The Hawkins kids face an unimaginable force of&nbsp;
darkness as Season 4 transitions into Season 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:26.080
but that doesn't mean their personal lives are&nbsp;
completely lost in the shuffle. That's perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.600
clearest in the story of Robin, who&nbsp;
reveals a crush on a fellow student&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:34.080
named Vickie at the beginning of the season, then&nbsp;
sees things come a bit full circle by the end.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.560
In Episode 8, Robin learns that Vickie has a&nbsp;
boyfriend from out of town. But one episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.000
later, when she finds herself volunteering&nbsp;
beside her crush at Hawkins High School,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.640
she learns that they broke up. Robin and the newly&nbsp;
single Vickie are left to bond in a real way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.120
making sandwiches for refugees of the earthquake&nbsp;
and laughing and joking together. Right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.320
it's hard to imagine what anyone's life&nbsp;
will look like at the end of this fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.920
but Robin seems closer than ever to&nbsp;
the kind of happy ending she deserves.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.600
Jonathan Byers and his girlfriend, Nancy Wheeler,&nbsp;
are separated by geography for much of the fourth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.760
season, but there's also something else in the way&nbsp;
of their relationship. Since moving to California,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:11.200
Jonathan has developed doubts about his&nbsp;
ability to ever be enough for Nancy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:15.200
particularly since he won't be going to&nbsp;
the same college she's hoping to attend.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:19.760
Meanwhile, back in Hawkins, Nancy is very&nbsp;
aware of how distant Jonathan's been,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:25.360
and that awareness coincides with the re-emergence&nbsp;
of Steve Harrington in her life. As they battle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:29.520
Vecna together, Nancy realizes that Steve&nbsp;
has grown a lot since they broke up. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.760
seems like a reconciliation might be in the&nbsp;
cards, but then Jonathan returns to Hawkins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.960
putting whatever might have happened on pause. We&nbsp;
don't know what that means for Season 5 just yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:42.480
but it's pretty clear that something&nbsp;
has to give in this love triangle.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.560
Joyce Byers and Jim Hopper spend most of&nbsp;
Season 4 trying to get back to each other.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.560
This is triggered when Joyce receives a message&nbsp;
from Hopper that reveals he's being held in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:55.600
Soviet prison. Joyce finally finds her way to&nbsp;
the prison, only to find that Hopper's life is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.600 --> 00:04:00.080
in a fresh kind of danger. It's only at the very&nbsp;
end of the season, as they're working to find a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.640
way to get back to America, that the two can&nbsp;
come together as a proper couple once again.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.400
The happy reunion doesn't hold out for long.&nbsp;
Hopper and Joyce make it back to the States&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.400
in time to find that the kids' fight against&nbsp;
the Upside Down has gone very wrong. Hawkins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:17.760
is now engulfed in a full-on disaster as rifts&nbsp;
open up across the town. The big question as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:22.560
we head into Season 5 is just how Hopper and&nbsp;
Joyce will make it through this fight intact.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:26.240
They lost each other once already. Now they have&nbsp;
to fight to make sure it doesn't happen again.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:31.520
All of the Hawkins kids are going through their&nbsp;
own major struggles in "Stranger Things 4," but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.680
Will Byers is going through one of the&nbsp;
hardest rough patches of his young life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:38.800
in part because he's doing&nbsp;
much of his struggling alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:42.560
It's been speculated ever since a key&nbsp;
moment in Season 3 that Will is gay.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:45.120
"El's not stupid. It's not my&nbsp;
fault you don't like girls."

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.480
Fans think that eventually,&nbsp;
he'll come out to his friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:54.640
and perhaps even reveal that he's in&nbsp;
love with his best friend, Mike Wheeler.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:59.520
In Season 4, we get more than one moment in&nbsp;
which Will seems to allude to his secret.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:04.880
In one very potent moment near the end of the&nbsp;
season, it seems like he's almost going to say it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:10.160
but he keeps silent out of concern for the larger&nbsp;
fight. Will's personal narrative remains stalled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.960
but it's clear that he's aching to tell someone&nbsp;
something about the secret he's keeping.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:19.840
Then there's Will's other inner turmoil,&nbsp;
something that hasn't been addressed directly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:24.560
since Season 2. Will still has at least&nbsp;
some connection to the Upside Down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:28.880
thanks to his possession by the Mind&nbsp;
Flayer. Once Vecna launches his invasion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:33.040
Will's been feeling it more and more. Will he&nbsp;
be able to hold himself together in the fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:38.240
to come, or is he destined for an inner battle&nbsp;
that's just as dangerous as the external one?

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:43.840
Near the end of "Stranger Things 4," Eleven makes&nbsp;
a devastating discovery about her "Papa," Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:49.440
Martin Brenner. She realizes, as Brenner pushes&nbsp;
her to stay in his secret lab and cultivate her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:54.320
powers even further, that the experiments she&nbsp;
remembers from Hawkins Lab were never about her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.320 --> 00:06:00.000
They were always about using her to get closer to&nbsp;
Henry. He was Brenner's first patient who Eleven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.480
sent to the Upside Down. In that hellish place, he&nbsp;
transformed into the creature the kids call Vecna.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:10.080
"Sometimes, Papa doesn't tell the truth."

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:16.080
It's a major moment of catharsis for Eleven,&nbsp;
who realizes that the problem was never her and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.000
her powers, but it's also an interesting&nbsp;
wrinkle in the ongoing saga of what was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:24.480
going on at Hawkins Lab. It's clear in&nbsp;
Season 4 that there are still plenty of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:28.240
dark forces within the U.S. government who&nbsp;
are squabbling over the nature of the lab,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:33.440
the Upside Down, and Eleven herself.&nbsp;
What's less clear is whether or not anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:37.920
else knew about what Brenner was really&nbsp;
trying to achieve. If someone did know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:43.200
are they out there trying to finish his work?&nbsp;
Does anyone else know what Henry has become? These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:47.920
are questions that could have major implications&nbsp;
for what's coming in the final season.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:52.960
About halfway through Season 4, Dr. Martin Brenner&nbsp;
and Dr. Sam Owens form an uneasy alliance with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:57.360
the shared goal of getting Eleven's powers back to&nbsp;
full strength through the use of the NINA machine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:01.840
By the end of the season, they're at odds again,&nbsp;
as Owens tries to let Eleven leave to help her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:07.200
friends, and Brenner is determined to keep her in&nbsp;
the lab longer to try and reach One in the Upside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:12.720
Down. Then the entire operation is disrupted when&nbsp;
Lt. Col. Sullivan and his troops arrive, killing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:18.240
Brenner, capturing Owens, and trying to end the&nbsp;
operation once and for all by killing Eleven.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:23.360
By the end of the season, Eleven is a fugitive&nbsp;
from the evil forces in the human world pursuing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.560
her, who wants her not just contained, but dead.&nbsp;
This explains why she's going back into hiding in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.720
Hopper's cabin at the end of the season, but&nbsp;
what we still don't know is just how far the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:38.080
government will go to capture her, especially now&nbsp;
that rifts have opened all over Hawkins. It's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:43.840
conflict that's arguably just as important to her&nbsp;
survival as the fight against the Upside Down.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:49.200
The end of "Stranger Things 4" reveals&nbsp;
many things, and not all of them come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:53.440
from the United States. During the process&nbsp;
of escaping from Hopper's Soviet prison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:58.560
Hopper and Joyce discover a secret lab&nbsp;
full of preserved Demogorgons and Demodogs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:04.800
as well as a chamber full of swirling particles&nbsp;
the Soviets dub "The Shadow." This strange entity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:08.800
is later revealed to be the dark material&nbsp;
that makes up the Mind Flayer. By the end of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:14.400
the season the facility is basically destroyed,&nbsp;
but its presence, and Brenner's insistence that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:19.280
his experiments were all about fighting the&nbsp;
Soviets, raises some interesting questions.

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:23.760
The Soviet government has its own operation&nbsp;
tied to the Upside Down, perhaps geared toward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:27.440
the weaponization of its creatures for a&nbsp;
fight against the West. What remains to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:32.480
be seen now is how that fight will progress&nbsp;
now that the prison facility is destroyed.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:36.160
In an effort to defeat Vecna&nbsp;
before he can invade Hawkins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:40.960
Max Mayfield stages a daring,&nbsp;
self-sacrificing trap for the creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:45.440
using her previous connection to him to lure&nbsp;
him out. After some coaxing, the plan works,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:50.720
but what doesn't work quite as well were the&nbsp;
parts of the plan surrounding Max's effort.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:56.320
She's able to lure Vecna in and hide in a happy&nbsp;
memory for a while, but the Upside Down's pressure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:01.040
on her friends means that the plot to kill&nbsp;
Vecna is delayed, and Max is caught in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:05.680
same psychic force that killed three other&nbsp;
Hawkins teenagers. By the end of the battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:10.640
Vecna is driven away, but Max is dead,&nbsp;
revived only by the force of Eleven's powers.

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:15.520
At the end of the season, Max is in a coma in&nbsp;
a hospital bed, her limbs broken, her sight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:20.640
apparently gone, and worse, her consciousness&nbsp;
seemingly unreachable. Eleven tries to go into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:26.160
her mind and find her, to search for some sign&nbsp;
that Max is still in there somewhere, and isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:32.560
able to locate her. So where is Max? It's a big,&nbsp;
potentially devastating question for Season 5.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:37.840
The final two episodes of "Stranger Things&nbsp;
4" reveal several new elements of the show's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:42.000
backstory, including how Vecna began&nbsp;
to shape the Upside Down to his will.

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:48.680
"I want you to tell her everything you see."

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:53.280
It's revealed through the discussion of his&nbsp;
backstory that once he was sent to the Upside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:58.720
Down by Eleven's powers, he wandered the landscape&nbsp;
until he found the Shadow. From there, he sculpted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:04.960
it into the Mind Flayer, making him the real&nbsp;
power behind the entire invasion of Hawkins.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:10.000
Even with that reveal, there's a good deal&nbsp;
we still don't know about the Upside Down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:14.720
It seems that many of the dimension's creatures,&nbsp;
including Demogorgons, were already inhabitants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:20.560
when Vecna got there. Now they're all part of&nbsp;
an extended hive mind of which he is the master,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:25.520
with the Shadow retaining a sort of symbiotic&nbsp;
connection to his will. So what is the Shadow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:29.040
why does it work for Vecna, and what&nbsp;
does that mean for the larger fight?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:33.520
There's still so much we don't know about&nbsp;
the nature of this other dimension, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:37.040
that feels like one of the biggest&nbsp;
open questions going into Season 5.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:42.240
At the end of Part One of "Stranger Things 4,"&nbsp;
Nancy Wheeler makes a shocking discovery about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:46.560
the Upside Down, or at least about the version&nbsp;
of Hawkins that exists within the Upside Down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:51.840
The entire landscape is frozen in time, a&nbsp;
version of Hawkins as it existed in 1983&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:55.920
when Eleven first opened the gate in the&nbsp;
Lab and released the first Demogorgon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.920 --> 00:11:00.640
It seems that somehow, at that moment,&nbsp;
a duplicate version of Hawkins emerged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:03.600
in the Upside Down landscape,&nbsp;
only to remain frozen in time.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:05.120
"We're in the past."

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:11.520
At the moment, it's not clear what that means.&nbsp;
It's possible that Eleven's powers accidentally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:15.760
created a weird mirror image of Hawkins Lab and&nbsp;
the surrounding town at the moment she opened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:20.320
the gate. It could have something to do with&nbsp;
Vecna's invasion plans. Whatever's going on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.520
it's clear that the mirror image&nbsp;
of Hawkins in the Upside Down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:28.480
will remain an intriguing centerpiece of&nbsp;
the conflict going forward into Season 5.

